🐛 Bug
Right now, softmax (and logsoftmax) save input for backward computation:
//torch/csrc/autograd/generated/VariableTypeEverything.cpp
Tensor _log_softmax(const Tensor & self, int64_t dim, bool half_to_float) {
  auto& self_ = unpack(self, "self", 0);
  auto _any_requires_grad = compute_requires_grad( self );
  (void)_any_requires_grad;
  std::shared_ptr<LogSoftmaxBackward> grad_fn;
  if (_any_requires_grad) {
    grad_fn = std::shared_ptr<LogSoftmaxBackward>(new LogSoftmaxBackward(), deleteNode);
    grad_fn->set_next_edges(collect_next_edges( self ));
    grad_fn->self_ = SavedVariable(self, false);
    grad_fn->dim = dim;
  }
  ...
}
However, the backward implementation for softmax (softmax_backward_cuda and sofmax_backward_cpu) don't use their input argument at all, instead relying on the output argument!



